cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Yang"
    given-names: "Cheng-Ying"
  - family-names: "Rodrigues Mimbrero"
    given-names: "Marcos"
title: "PREPFIRE: An Open-Source Framework for Automated Fire Simulation Input Preparation"
version: "0.1.2"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20083868"
date-released: "2026-05-15"
abstract: >
  PREPFIRE (PREParation for FIRE simulation) is a Python package for preparing
  materials for fire simulation and analysis, providing tools for processing fire
  data, weather conditions, and landscape characteristics. The package implements
  a complete pipeline for fire risk assessment and simulation. Output files are
  intended for fire spread simulation using the FlamMap algorithm.
keywords:
  - fire-simulation
  - wildfire
  - fire-weather
  - ERA5
  - FlamMap
  - landscape
  - automation
  - open-source
license: "GPL-3.0-only"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CYglume/PREPFIRE"
url: "https://github.com/CYglume/PREPFIRE"
